    "difficulty": "easy",
    "caseText": "\n\n<p><strong>Nova Enterprises Ltd. (NEL)</strong> is a multi-business Indian conglomerate with diversified commercial interests spanning cement manufacturing, specialized specialty chemicals, and digital cloud enterprise software. At the apex level, the Group Executive Board formulates decisions that affect the entire multi-business portfolio.</p>\n<p>The conglomerate’s governance structure operates distinctly across three recognized strategic hierarchy levels:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Corporate-Level Strategy:</strong> Spearheaded by the Chairman and Group CFO, defining the overall corporate scope, portfolio balance, capital allocation among divisions, M&A acquisitions, divestitures, and group-wide capital structure.</li>\n  <li><strong>Business-Level (SBU) Strategy:</strong> Led by respective SBU Chief Executives, defining competitive strategy within specific industries (e.g., whether to pursue Cost Leadership in the commodity cement market or Product Differentiation in specialty chemicals).</li>\n  <li><strong>Functional-Level Strategy:</strong> Formulated by functional heads (such as Treasury, Working Capital Management, Procurement, and Tax Planning), establishing detailed operational roadmaps that support the SBU and corporate strategies.</li>\n</ol>\n<p>During a strategic alignment review, the Group CFO noted that several capital misallocations occurred because SBU managers evaluated projects based on their own narrow divisional targets rather than corporate-wide value creation.</p>\n",
