    "caseText": "Godavari Specialty Chemicals Ltd. (GSCL) is experiencing high-growth expansion into export markets for active pharmaceutical intermediates. An equity analyst at an institutional asset management firm is evaluating GSCL using the Fuller-Hsu H-Model to capture a realistic, smooth linear transition in dividend growth.\n\n1. Growth & Dividend Parameters for GSCL:\n- Current dividend just paid at t = 0 (D_0) = ₹20.00 per share.\n- Initial extraordinary growth rate (g_a) = 18.00% per annum.\n- Transition Horizon (2H) = 8 years (meaning the half-life transition parameter H = 4 years).\n- Over the 8-year transition period, the growth rate declines in a smooth linear fashion from the initial rate of 18.00% down to the terminal long-term sustainable growth rate of 6.00%.\n- Long-term stable growth rate (g_n) from Year 8 onward = 6.00% per annum.\n\n2. Cost of Capital Data:\n- Risk-free rate (R_f) = 6.50% per annum.\n- Market risk premium = 5.00% per annum.\n- GSCL's equity beta = 0.70.\n- Cost of Equity (K_e) = 6.50% + 0.70 × 5.00% = 10.00% per annum.\n\n3. The H-Model Formula:\nP_0 = [D_0 × (1 + g_n) / (K_e - g_n)] + [D_0 × H × (g_a - g_n) / (K_e - g_n)]\nwhere the first term represents the baseline intrinsic value under normal growth, and the second term represents the growth premium contributed by the extraordinary growth phase.",
