    "caseText": "Saraswati Consumer Appliances Ltd. (SCAL) is preparing its annual corporate valuation report for strategic planning. The corporate finance team compiles operating and cash flow data for the latest financial year:\n\n1. Income Statement & Operational Data (Amounts in ₹ Crore):\n- Operating Profit (EBIT) = ₹200.00 Crore.\n- Effective Corporate Tax Rate = 25.00%.\n- Depreciation and Amortization = ₹40.00 Crore.\n- Gross Capital Expenditure (Capex) = ₹50.00 Crore.\n- Investment in Non-Cash Net Working Capital (ΔNWC) = ₹10.00 Crore.\n- Annual Interest Expense = ₹30.00 Crore.\n- Net New Debt Incurred (New Debt Issued minus Debt Repaid) = ₹15.00 Crore.\n\n2. Corporate Capital Structure:\n- The company's Weighted Average Cost of Capital (WACC) is 10.00% per annum.\n- The company's Cost of Equity (K_e) is 13.00% per annum.\n\nThe investment committee wants to calculate both Free Cash Flow to Firm (FCFF) and Free Cash Flow to Equity (FCFE).",
