    "caseText": "\n\n<p><strong>Bharat Infrastructure Finance Corporation (BIFC)</strong> originated a ₹1,200 Crore pool of annuity receivables from operational toll road projects. To institutionalize the securitization, BIFC established <strong>BIDST 2024-TR1</strong> and appointed independent professional entities to manage key functions across the structure.</p>\n<p>The institutional structure includes:</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><strong>Originator (BIFC):</strong> Transfers the asset pool and continues to manage borrower relationships.</li>\n  <li><strong>SPV Trustee:</strong> Holds legal title to the assets in trust for the benefit of certificate holders, monitoring adherence to the waterfall mechanism.</li>\n  <li><strong>Servicer / Collection Agent:</strong> Responsible for collecting toll revenues, tracking delinquencies, and depositing collections into the Trust Escrow Account.</li>\n  <li><strong>Credit Rating Agency (CRA):</strong> Evaluates credit risk, structures credit enhancement thresholds, and assigns ratings to the issued instruments.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>To obtain an investment-grade rating of 'AAA(SO)' (Structured Obligation) for the Senior Pass Through Certificates (PTCs), the transaction incorporates a combination of <strong>Internal</strong> and <strong>External Credit Enhancement</strong> mechanisms.</p>\n",
