    "caseText": "\n\n<p><strong>Takshila Fixed Income Quantitative Analytics (TFIQA)</strong> specializes in advanced valuation modeling of mortgage-backed securities (MBS). TFIQA is analyzing a ₹1,000.00 Crore residential mortgage pool where borrowers hold an embedded prepayment option. In analyzing the valuation spreads of these securities over the spot yield curve, the Senior Financial Engineer, Dr. Arvind Swamy, contrasted three spread metrics:</p>\n<ol>\n  <li><strong>Nominal Spread:</strong> The difference between the MBS Yield to Maturity (YTM) and the yield of a benchmark G-Sec of identical maturity.</li>\n  <li><strong>Zero-Volatility Spread (Z-Spread):</strong> The constant parallel spread added to the entire zero-coupon G-Sec spot curve that equates the present value of the MBS cash flows (assuming a static prepayment rate) to its market price.</li>\n  <li><strong>Option-Adjusted Spread (OAS):</strong> The spread generated through Monte Carlo interest rate simulations that accounts for the borrower's embedded prepayment option. OAS measures the pure credit and liquidity spread after removing the cost of the embedded option:\n  \\[\n  \\text{Option Cost} = \\text{Z-Spread} - \\text{OAS}\n  \\]</li>\n</ol>\n<p>For the mortgage pool under review, the current market price of the security reflects a <strong>Z-Spread of 185 basis points (1.85%)</strong>. Stochastic yield curve simulation reveals an <strong>Option-Adjusted Spread (OAS) of 115 basis points (1.15%)</strong>. Furthermore, the prepayment behavior is modeled using the <strong>Constant Prepayment Rate (CPR)</strong> of <strong>12.00% per annum</strong>.</p>\n",
