    "caseText": "Indo-Euro Green Energy Ltd. (IEGEL), an Indian renewable power producer, is evaluating an investment in a commercial solar farm in Andalusia, Spain. The project requires a capital expenditure of €10,000,000 at t=0 and has a predictable operating life of 5 years.\n\nOperating Economics (Base-Case All-Equity):\n- Annual Unlevered Operating Cash Inflow after tax (assuming 100% equity financing): €2,800,000 p.a. for Years 1 through 5.\n- Unlevered Cost of Equity (\\(r_u\\)) appropriate for Spanish solar assets: 10.00% p.a.\n- Present Value Interest Factor of Annuity at 10% for 5 years: \\(\\text{PVIFA}(10\\%, 5) = 3.7908\\).\n\nFinancing Side Effects:\n- To finance the project, IEGEL secures €4,000,000 of project debt at a fixed interest rate of 6.00% p.a., with a bullet principal repayment at the end of Year 5.\n- Spanish Corporate Tax Rate: 25%.\n- Annual Interest Expense = \\(€4,000,000 \\times 0.060 = €240,000\\text{ p.a.}\\)\n- Annual Interest Tax Shield = \\(€240,000 \\times 0.25 = €60,000\\text{ p.a.}\\) for 5 years.\n- Present Value Interest Factor of Annuity at cost of debt (6%) for 5 years: \\(\\text{PVIFA}(6\\%, 5) = 4.2124\\).\n- Flotation / Issuance Costs of Debt and Equity: €150,000 (net of tax, incurred at t=0).\n\nIEGEL's Chief Financial Officer directs the corporate finance department to utilize Stewart Myers' Adjusted Present Value (APV) framework to evaluate the base-case NPV, value the interest tax shield, and establish the overall project viability.",
