        "explanation": "In Physical Cash Sweeping (Zero-Balancing), surplus balances are physically wired at end-of-day from participating subsidiary accounts to a central master concentration account, creating actual inter-company loans. In Notional Cash Pooling, funds remain physically in the separate bank accounts of each subsidiary; the bank notionally offsets debits and credits across the accounts to compute net interest, eliminating cross-border bank transfer fees and avoiding inter-company loan documentation."
