    "caseText": "GigaPower Infrastructure Ltd. (GPIL) is executing a mega solar transmission corridor. The CFO uses Alfred Rappaport's Shareholder Value Analysis (SVA) framework to measure shareholder value creation across the company's Competitive Advantage Period (Value Growth Duration). The 7 Rappaport Value Drivers established for the 5-year planning horizon are:\n\n1. Base Year (Year 0) Sales: ₹10,000.00 Lakhs\n2. Annual Sales Growth Rate (g): 12.0% per annum\n3. Operating Profit Margin (OPM = EBIT / Sales): 20.0%\n4. Cash Income Tax Rate (t): 25.0%\n5. Incremental Fixed Capital Investment Rate (FCIR = Incremental Fixed Capital / Incremental Sales): 15.0%\n6. Incremental Working Capital Investment Rate (WCIR = Incremental Working Capital / Incremental Sales): 10.0%\n7. Cost of Capital (WACC): 11.0%\n\nBalance Sheet & Terminal Parameters:\n• Value Growth Duration (Competitive Advantage Period): 5 Years\n• At the end of Year 5, competitive advantage ceases. Under Rappaport's perpetuity assumption for residual value, incremental investments after Year 5 earn exactly their cost of capital (Zero NPV reinvestment), so Terminal Cash Flow equals Year 5 NOPAT in perpetuity: \\$\\text{Terminal Value}_5 = \\frac{\\text{NOPAT}_5}{\\text{WACC}}\\$.\n• Outstanding Debt at Valuation Date: ₹4,500.00 Lakhs; Marketable Liquid Securities: ₹800.00 Lakhs\n• Number of Equity Shares: 10,000,000 shares.",
