    "caseText": "Orion Speciality Chemicals Ltd. (OSCL) is a heavily levered chemical manufacturing company facing potential financial distress. To assess the true economic value of the distressed equity and debt, the restructuring committee applies the Black-Scholes-Merton (BSM) structural model of corporate debt.\n\nModel Parameters & Firm Data:\n• Current Fair Value of Total Firm Assets (\\$V_0\\$): ₹10,000.00 Lakhs\n• Annualized Volatility of Firm Asset Value (\\$\\sigma_V\\$): 30.0% per annum (0.30)\n• Capital Structure: OSCL has a single class of zero-coupon debt maturing in exactly 2 years (\\$T = 2.0\\$ years) with a Face Value (\\$D\\$) of ₹11,000.00 Lakhs.\n• Continuous Risk-free Rate of Interest (\\$r\\$): 6.0% per annum (0.06)\n\nMerton Framework Formulation:\nEquity is valued as a European call option on the total assets of the firm with strike price equal to the face value of debt:\n\\$\\$E = V_0 \\cdot N(d_1) - D \\cdot e^{-rT} \\cdot N(d_2)\\$\\$\nWhere:\n\\$\\$d_1 = \\frac{\\ln(V_0 / D) + (r + 0.5 \\sigma_V^2)T}{\\sigma_V \\sqrt{T}}\\$\\$\n\\$\\$d_2 = d_1 - \\sigma_V \\sqrt{T}\\$\\$\n\nCumulative Normal Distribution Table Values:\n• \\$\\ln(10,000 / 11,000) = \\ln(0.90909) = -0.09531\\$\n• Term: \\$(0.06 + 0.5 \\times 0.30^2) \\times 2 = (0.06 + 0.045) \\times 2 = 0.105 \\times 2 = 0.210\\$\n• Numerator of \\$d_1\\$: \\$-0.09531 + 0.210 = +0.11469\\$\n• Denominator: \\$\\sigma_V \\sqrt{T} = 0.30 \\times \\sqrt{2} = 0.30 \\times 1.41421 = 0.42426\\$\n• \\$d_1 = +0.11469 / 0.42426 = +0.2703\\$; \\$N(d_1) = N(0.27) = 0.6064\\$\n• \\$d_2 = 0.2703 - 0.42426 = -0.1540\\$; \\$N(d_2) = N(-0.15) = 0.4404\\$\n• Present value of debt at risk-free rate: \\$D \\cdot e^{-rT} = 11,000 \\times e^{-(0.06 \\times 2)} = 11,000 \\times e^{-0.12} = 11,000 \\times 0.88692 = ₹9,756.12\\text{ Lakhs}\\$.",
