    "topic": "Takeover Defensive Strategies, Reverse Mergers & SPACs",
    "caseText": "Shield Pharmaceuticals Ltd. (SPL) has become the target of an unsolicited hostile takeover bid by Raider Capital Holdings (RCH). RCH has acquired a 14% creeping stake in SPL on the open market and is threatening an aggressive tender offer to replace the board.\n\nSPL's board convenes with its M&A legal advisors to evaluate anti-takeover defensive strategies:\n• Strategy 1 (Shareholder Rights Plan / Poison Pill): Adopting a 'Flip-in' rights plan that triggers if any hostile party crosses a 15% beneficial ownership threshold without board approval, entitling all shareholders (except the hostile bidder) to purchase SPL shares at a 50% discount to market price.\n• Strategy 2 (White Knight Defense): Inviting Global Healthcare Corp., a friendly strategic partner, to launch a competing bid at a higher premium to acquire 100% of SPL.\n• Strategy 3 (Pac-Man Defense): SPL launching a counter-takeover tender offer to purchase a controlling equity stake in RCH.\n• Strategy 4 (Crown Jewels Defense): Selling or transferring SPL's patented blockbuster diabetes drug division to a friendly partner to make SPL unattractive to RCH.",
